WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.160
- Do you think we'll
ever see another moment

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:04.560
like GameStop in retail investing?

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.330
- I think what GameStop showed

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:09.450
is that retail investors

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:12.960
are a really, really
important part of the markets

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.660
and a constituency that can't be ignored.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.370
And a big part of that is due

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:20.370
to the impact of
Robinhood and the mission.

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:21.720
- [Hannah] Robinhood was founded

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.090
with the goal of democratizing finance.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.400
It's easy-to-use app made trading free

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.740
and spurred a generation
of retail investors

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:31.380
to jump into stocks, including GameStop.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:33.480
- GameStop's shares is
absolutely going nuts.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.550
- [Reporter] The weapon of
choice for these new traders

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:37.680
are platforms like Robinhood.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.870
- But since then, Robinhood has lost

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:42.090
roughly half of its active users.

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:45.720
Now, CEO Vlad Tenev is
focused on growing Robinhood

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:48.390
into something more
than just a trading app.

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:50.970
WSJ caught up with him at
the company's headquarters

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:52.710
to hear how he hopes to make Robinhood

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:55.230
the most trusted name in finance.

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:57.990
What was the moment you knew
that you created something

00:00:57.990 --> 00:00:59.970
that changed how everyday people invest?

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:03.150
- End of 2019, when basically

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:07.049
every single discount
brokerage in quick succession

00:01:07.049 --> 00:01:09.300
lowered their commissions to zero

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.910
and essentially replicated our model.

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:16.140
And at the time I remember
being a little bit nervous.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:17.820
You know, you get all these questions.

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:19.290
What does this mean for the company?

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:20.970
Like, we really have to up our game

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:23.768
to continue to differentiate
with our customers.

00:01:23.768 --> 00:01:26.079
- What would you say is the next frontier

00:01:26.079 --> 00:01:27.373
for democratizing finance?

00:01:27.373 --> 00:01:29.040
- We've done a great job

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.890
with trading and self-directed investing.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:35.460
Now the next area we're
tackling is retirement.

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:38.790
And so we're the first to offer a 1% match

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:40.860
in an individual retirement account.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:43.650
And it's a big part of our journey

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:46.800
from helping customers
get started investing

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:49.620
to managing all of their finances

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:52.230
and providing service across
all of their financial needs.

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:54.079
- A lot of the investors I talk to

00:01:54.079 --> 00:01:57.360
do still associate Robinhood with GameStop

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:59.880
and the trading restrictions
during that period.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:01.350
So what do you say to customers

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:04.369
who lost trust in
Robinhood during that time?

00:02:04.369 --> 00:02:09.369
- I understand that perception,

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:12.120
but what I'd point to is

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:15.300
the amazing progress Robinhood has made

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.950
and continues to make.

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:18.300
- [Hannah] Robinhood has gone from an app

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:21.180
that blasted confetti
after a user's first trade

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:24.827
to a company offering retirement
accounts and 4.9% interest

00:02:24.827 --> 00:02:27.720
on uninvested cash for
premium subscribers.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.370
The disruptive brokerage

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:32.160
is looking more like a
traditional finance firm

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:36.090
and with its acquisition of
credit card startup X1 this year

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:38.220
Robinhood has a credit card in the works.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:40.470
- We think credit's a huge opportunity.

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:44.100
There's so many customers
that are either underserved

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:47.850
or not adequately served with
their credit needs these days.

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:50.820
And I think Robinhood can
play a huge role there

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:52.710
in democratizing that space

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:55.920
and make it easier and
a much better experience

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.780
to offer those products.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.280
- [Hannah] This pivot to new offerings

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:01.020
is part of the company's strategy

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:03.120
to attract and hold onto users

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:05.040
in this high rate environment.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.950
Trading stocks isn't as
popular as it used to be.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:10.860
Investors now have other
options for good returns.

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:12.420
- One of the really interesting things

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:16.800
about the investing business
is it does tend to be cyclical

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.720
with growth coming in waves.

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:21.180
In times where interest rates are low

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:24.450
like they were in in 2020 and in 2021,

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:27.390
you see a lot of interest
in investing in the market.

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:30.780
And in other times there's
just less interest.

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:33.090
And so what we look at there is

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:35.820
how can we improve our product and service

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:39.270
and continue to innovate for
our traders and investors

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:41.790
with things like 24-hour market,

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:44.385
which makes us the
first in the US to offer

00:03:44.385 --> 00:03:47.880
round the clock trading
for single name stocks.

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:49.590
- [Hannah] While getting
into retirement accounts

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:53.880
looks more traditional,
24-hour market is anything but.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:56.670
It's a big shift in how
users can trade stocks

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:58.980
like Amazon, Apple, and Tesla.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:03.980
- With 24-hour trading it just
seemed ludicrous to me that,

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:09.540
you know it's 2023 and
investing in the most liquid,

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:13.170
deepest markets in the
world, the US capital markets

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:16.680
is still tied to US east
coast working hours.

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:19.440
Everything is electronic elsewhere

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.110
and services are available
when people need them

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:26.400
and yet investing is
kind of this exception.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:29.070
And when we looked into it

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:30.990
we realized that there's no reason

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:32.700
that it had to be this way.

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:35.340
We could work with counterparties,

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:38.820
we could build the technology
to make that better.

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:42.750
And 24 Hour Market, which
launched a couple of months ago

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:44.820
is kind of the first
step in that direction.

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:47.040
So I think it's still very early to tell

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:49.560
what kind of impact
it'll have market wide.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:52.890
And I do believe in not too long

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:55.530
you'll see it become an industry standard

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:57.990
just like commission
free trading has become.

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:59.940
- If that does become
the industry standard

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:01.920
are there any risks you see involved?

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:04.350
- One thing that you have to remember is

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:06.480
we already have experience with assets

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:07.950
that trade round the clock.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:10.290
If you look at the cryptocurrency markets,

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:14.400
they trade 24/7 worldwide and you know,

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:16.350
we've been offering customers access

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:19.710
to crypto on the platform since 2018.

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:23.451
- Speaking of crypto, it's
obviously been a hot topic

00:05:23.451 --> 00:05:26.943
in the regulatory space
over the last year.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:31.350
As one of the first
brokerages to offer crypto,

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:33.690
are you committed to offering crypto

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:36.240
to US customers moving forward?

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:39.390
- Yeah, and I think
crypto is here to stay.

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:43.200
There's definitely been a
lack of regulatory clarity

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:47.580
and I think we're gonna
continue to work with lawmakers

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.770
and regulators to push forward there.

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:52.740
- Shares of Robinhood have
had a nice run up this year

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:54.930
but they're still down about 80%

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:57.690
from their record high from 2021.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:58.620
Do you think there's anything

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:01.500
the market is under
appreciating about Robinhood?

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:02.790
- Over a long time period

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:06.030
companies are valued on earnings growth

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:09.420
and the stock price tends to track that.

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:12.780
It might not happen for various
reasons in the short term.

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:15.750
What we can continue to
do is serve our customers,

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:18.660
improve our products, grow market share

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:21.600
but there's always more to do.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:24.120
- Do you still think
Robinhood is an underdog

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:26.400
in the financial services industry?

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:27.233
- I do.

00:06:27.233 --> 00:06:29.983
Robinhood's been able to
accomplish quite a bit

00:06:29.983 --> 00:06:33.600
over the past 10 years
since we got the idea for it

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:37.200
but it's still a very young
company and I do believe

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:38.820
you know, 10 years from now

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:40.560
looking back to where we are today,

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:42.540
we'll really appreciate that

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:44.760
we're still in the early
stages of Robinhood

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:46.230
and there's so much to do.

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:47.940
- [Hannah] Even as Tenev looks ahead,

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:50.040
a reminder of Robinhood's association

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:52.950
with the GameStop craze is
out in theaters this month.

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:55.653
- And that stock is GameStop.

00:06:55.653 --> 00:06:57.900
- Have you seen the movie "Dumb Money"

00:06:57.900 --> 00:06:59.760
about the GameStop saga

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:02.220
in which you are a character in the movie?

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:03.630
- I have not seen it.

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:07.800
Having a movie created
that has Robinhood featured

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:10.350
is I think a really important testament

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:11.760
to the impact we've had

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:14.790
but you have to remember
the movie's fiction

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:19.170
and nobody sort of talked to us about it.

00:07:19.170 --> 00:07:24.090
So I think I'm expecting it
to be a fictionalized account

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:26.668
and hopefully some of it's true.

00:07:26.668 --> 00:07:29.251
(gentle music)

